WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.400
-You look good, bud.
You look good.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.634
-Thank you, sir.
-Welcome, welcome, welcome.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:05.934
Thanks for being here.
How does it feel to be on

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:08.100
one of the biggest shows,
I mean, ever?

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.267
Right now, that's -- it's --

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:11.868
"Yellowstone," is --
it's beyond anything.

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:13.501
It's unbelievable.
-How does it feel?

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:15.634
Pretty damn good.
-Yeah, it does, yeah.

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:17.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
Yeah.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.901
-How does it feel?

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.934
-Last season premiere had over
14 million viewers, by the way.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:24.133
-Not too shabby.
-No, it's not shabby at all.

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:25.300
-Yeah.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.100
-And everyone's a fan
of the show.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.868
And I was talking
to you backstage and I said,

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:31.367
"Is there any fans you were
like, 'Oh, I didn't know

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:32.634
they would be a fan.'"

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:35.868
But you were like,
"Well, Drake is a giant fan."

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.734
And I was like, "Is that right?"
-Yeah, that's a bit strange.

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:40.000
I didn't see that one coming.
-No.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.067
-No, a buddy of mine, Jake,
said Drake, you know,

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.968
wants a pair of boots
for his birthday,

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:47.501
and I was like,
"He actually rides?"

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:48.567
Like,
"What are you talking about?"

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.067
And he's like,
"No, no, he doesn't ride.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.167
He just wants a pair of boots,
and he wants you to ride

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:53.467
in the boots
and give them to him."

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:55.400
And I was like, "Fair enough."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.300
-That's what Drake does.
-Yeah, I mean, you know.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.801
-And you actually did it.
Here you go.

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:00.968
-Yeah.
-You sent him a pair of boots.

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.434
There you go.
"Happy birthday!

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:03.434
Rip."
There you go.

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:04.667
You're a man of your word.

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.801
-I might call on you, Drake.
-Yeah.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:11.734
-I might call on you.
-Drake's actually a good actor.

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:13.367
Do you know -- maybe --
-I'm not aware of that.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.067
-He is, yeah.
"Degrassi" is where he

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.501
kind of got his start.
-Oh, really?

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.334
-Yeah.
I'm just saying if there's room

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:19.834
for a cameo,
would you be down for that?

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.701
-Hell yeah.
-A Drake cameo?

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.434
-Bring it.
-Yeah, let's do it.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:24.834
Drake in "Yellowstone"?

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:27.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:30.067
You're great as Rip Wheeler.

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:33.267
Was it --
Was there any other character

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.701
or anything you went in
to read for,

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.634
you're like, "Oh, I think
I should do this one,"

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:38.234
or are you like,
"No, this is my character"?

00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:40.567
-You know what?
I looked at the Dutton,

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.434
you know, family, and, to me,
I thought they were all great.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.801
Obviously, you know,
Wes is phenomenal and Luke.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.801
But what resonated to me
was Rip.

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:50.100
And, you know,
he has a darkness that I love

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.868
and a passion with Beth.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:53.400
And I just thought, you know,
this is a character

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.400
that not only can grow, but
there's tons of colors in him.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.133
So -- and as an actor, that's
kind of what you dream of, so...

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:00.901
-Yeah.
I mean, did you know

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:03.601
that your character would be --
become a heartthrob?

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.100
-No, Jimmy.
-Yeah.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.467
-I didn't know that.
-Yeah, you're kind of --

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:07.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:08.834
-That's a bit of a shocker.

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.934
-That's --
That's kind of fun.

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:12.601
People are dressing up
as you for Halloween.

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:13.734
I'm sure you saw that.

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:15.567
-I saw that in New York,
actually, the other day.

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:16.868
There was a guy
walking down the street.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:18.367
I rolled down the window,
I go, "Rip!"

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.234
And he turned, he goes, "Yeah!"

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:21.334
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:22.634
Not bad.
-I was like, "Okay.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:23.634
He doesn't even know it's me."

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.067
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:27.367
If you heard someone drive past
you and yell, "Rip"...

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:28.400
-Yeah.
-Yeah, and you said, "yeah,"

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.901
that was actually Rip.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.501
-Yeah, that was --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:34.901
Actually, Chris Pratt
dressed up as Rip Wheeler.

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.601
-Who is that?
-Yeah.

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:38.100
You ever heard of this guy?
-Oh, my God.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.801
Hold on a second.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:42.868
Looking good, kid.
-Yeah, he is looking good.

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:44.200
Looking good there, guy.
-Well done.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.501
-Yeah.
-Well done.

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:46.834
-Look at -- Look at this.

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.701
This is how you grow a beard,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.334
That's the real deal.
-He's doing all right.

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:53.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
You're doing all right.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:55.501
You're a little patchy here.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:57.234
We could probably
stipple in a little bit,

00:02:57.234 --> 00:02:58.434
maybe paint it in a little bit.

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:00.567
-Yeah, you can't even
look at these sides here.

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:01.934
-Don't worry.
I've got someone in the back.

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:04.300
He'll take care of you.
-Something to fill it in here.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.167
Next time you come on, I'm gonna
have a full-on fake beard.

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.734
-Let it go, babe.
-Really?

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:09.868
-It's Christmas.
It's the holiday season.

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:11.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:13.801
-Do you think I'm --
maybe I'm -- am I Santa?

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:14.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:16.133
-Babe, you can be
whatever you want.

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:18.634
-Yeah, exactly.
Do you groom your stuff?

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:20.701
Do you, like, comb it and --
-No, I let it go.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:23.234
-Do people -- I found that
people started giving me stuff,

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:26.033
like combs and oils.
-No, no, no.

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:27.901
Don't do it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:29.534
-Try to be a man
and just let it go.

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:30.634
-What do you mean?
-It's okay.

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.334
-I think you oil it down.
-Mm.

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:34.534
-Maybe the ladies like it.
I don't know.

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:38.200
-Whoo!
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.000
-Is yours soft?
Does your wife like it?

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.200
-Yeah, touch it.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.767
-Ooh, yours is very soft.

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:45.601
[ Laughter and applause ]
Wow.

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:46.734
-Very sexual.
-Wow.

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:48.601
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:50.467
Let's write that into a scene
in "Yellowstone."

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.601
That's perfect.
I like that.

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:54.000
Oh, that was nice.
You're very soft.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.701
-"That was nice."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.701 --> 00:03:59.567
What are we doing?
-"What are we doing?" yeah.

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:02.100
Whoever thought we'd touch
each other's beards?

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.801
-In front of a bunch of people.
-Yeah, millions of people.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:05.267
-Yeah, I love that.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:07.467
Can we say what's going on in
season five in "Yellowstone"?

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:09.300
-Sure.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.534
What is --
-What is going on?

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:11.667
-That was --
I meant that as a question.

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.634
-Fair enough.
-Yeah.

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:15.367
-Well, this year,
there's more Beth and I,

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:16.868
which I hope everybody
is excited about.

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:18.434
-Of course.
-We're married now,

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:21.400
which is gonna be interesting.
-Yeah.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.000
-A lot more kind of
responsibility on Rip,

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.767
you know, obviously,
with John being the governor.

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:28.767
So more responsibility
as far as the ranch is concerned

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.534
and being the foreman
and running the ranch.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.701
And, you know,
Taylor did a phenomenal job,

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:34.367
again, writing this year.
-Yeah.

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:38.234
I don't remember your
background, but are you from --

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:40.133
Do you know how to ride a horse?
And...

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:42.334
-Born in Laurel Springs
on a ranch.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.634
-Oh, you did, yeah.
-And then Oregon, Florida,

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:46.100
back to California.
-No way.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.467
-And now Montana
and back to Florida.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:49.567
-Wow!
-So, yeah.

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:50.701
-Full circle.
-Yep.

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:52.000
-Yeah.
Show 'em how it's done.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.400
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Cole Hauser

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.634
in the season five premiere
of "Yellowstone."

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:57.467
Take a look at this.

00:04:57.467 --> 00:05:00.701
-And when this gets going
and this gets going, too --

00:05:00.701 --> 00:05:04.334
-But I robbed us
of so much time together,

00:05:04.334 --> 00:05:06.334
because I was...

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:14.033
It's still robbing us.

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.667
-Mm.
Whatever it took, I don't need.

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:17.934
I'm happy, Beth.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.734
With you, with life.
Everything's good.

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:23.934
-But we needed what I took.

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:27.501
-Listen, come here.
Come here.

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:28.968
Oh, baby.

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:33.133
[ Sighs ]

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:37.567
You need to find
somebody new to fight.

00:05:37.567 --> 00:05:39.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Cole Hauser, everybody.

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:41.334
Season five of "Yellowstone"

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:44.000
premieres November 13th
at 8:00 p.m.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.634
on Paramount network.

